@CLS@@X0DLIST MESSAGE HEADERS

@X0E[beg. msgs #]  Being the scan with this number message.  Default is forward,
               for reverse see the @X0D<@X0E-@X0D>@X0E command.

@X0D<@X0E+@X0D>@X0E  SCAN IN A FORWARD DIRECTION - Append to the beginning message number as
     in 762+.   You will begin scanning at 762 and go forward.

@X0D<@X0E-@X0D>@X0E  SCAN IN A REVERSE DIRECTION - append to the beginning message number as
     in 762-.  You will begin scanning at 762 and go backwards.

@X0D<@X0EA@X0D>@X0E  SCAN ALL SELECTED CONFERENCES - This will scanb all conferences that you
     have selected using the "SELECT" command or the "S" flag in the users
     record.

@X0D<@X0EALL@X0D>@X0E  SCAN ALL CONFERENCES - Scans all the conferences you are registered in
       whether you "SELECT"ed them or not.

@X0D<@X0EF@X0D>@X0E  MESSAGES FROM YOU - Only messages from you, the current user, will be
     displayed.

@X0D

<@X0EL@X0D>@X0E  BEGIN WITH THE LAST MESSAGE IN THE MESSAGE BASE - Sets the beginning
     message number to the last message in the base and goes backwards.

@X0D<@X0ENS@X0D>@X0E DISPLAY IN NON-STOP MODE - No "MORE" prompt.  Screen will scroll.

@X0D<@X0ES@X0D>@X0E  MESSAGES THAT HAVE NOT BEEN READ YET - Searches out only those messages
     you have not read yet.

@X0D<@X0ETS@X0D>@X0E MESSAGES THAT CONTAIN A PARTICULAR TEXT - You can specify message body
     text, TO, and FROM.  Use any word, phrase, or use Boolean search.

@X0D<@X0EUSER@X0D>@X0E  MESSAGES TO OR FROM A PARTICULAR USER - You must enter full user name
        as partial matches will not be recognized.

@X0D








STATUS CODES

@X0ENext to each message number is a status code.

[blank]  A public message such as ALL
*  A private msg not yet read by the addressee
+  A private msg read by the addressee
-  A public msg addressed to a specific person and read by that person
~  A "comment" to the sysop not yet read by the person in record #1
`  A "comment" to the sysop that has been read by the person in record #1
%  A msg protected by sender password that has not been read
^  A msg protected by sender password which has been read
!  A msg protected by group password which has not been read
#  A msg protected by group password which has been read
$  A message protected by group password that is addressed to ALL
@X07
